  "blocks": {
    ".github/copilot-instructions.md": "# Repository instructions\n\nThis project is an Angular workspace. Use standalone components and signals.\nRun `pnpm test` before proposing a change.\n\n<!-- surveyjs:start -->\n## SurveyJS\n\nInstalled in this project: `survey-angular-ui@3.0.1`, `survey-core@3.0.1`, `survey-creator-angular@3.0.1`, `survey-creator-core@3.0.1`. UI framework: **angular**.\n\nThe SurveyJS agent skills are installed in `.github/skills`. Read the skill that matches the task before writing or changing SurveyJS code — they carry the current v3 API and the mistakes to check generated code against:\n\n- [`surveyjs-brand-styling`](skills/surveyjs-brand-styling/SKILL.md) — Style a SurveyJS application so it matches a custom app design, design system, or brandbook\n- [`surveyjs-creator-customization`](skills/surveyjs-creator-customization/SKILL.md) — Embed and customize SurveyJS Survey Creator (the drag-and-drop form builder) in React, Angular, Vue, or vanilla JS\n- [`surveyjs-form-json`](skills/surveyjs-form-json/SKILL.md) — Author, edit, or debug SurveyJS survey/form JSON\n- [`surveyjs-integration`](skills/surveyjs-integration/SKILL.md) — Integrate the SurveyJS Form Library into React, Next.js, Angular, Vue, vanilla JS, or jQuery apps\n\nEverything between the `surveyjs:start` and `surveyjs:end` markers is regenerated by `survey-cli 0.1.0` (`npx survey-cli@latest init-agents`). Put your own notes outside the markers.\n<!-- surveyjs:end -->\n"
